  &lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;




Test Execution & Verification

Coordinate with ship’s Chief Bosun to suspend the Coast Guard water bag over deck[cite: 8].
Engage pumps and fill water bag, monitoring the digital load cell readout[cite: 8].
Slow pumps at 9,000 lbs tension and stop pumps at 10,000 lbs target tension[cite: 8].
Hold 10,000 lbs proof load for 1 full minute[cite: 8].




Load Sensor Readout Displaying 10,000 lbs Test Tension



Drain water bag and inspect reference hose clamp above clevis[cite: 8]. Verify zero clevis slippage occurred along the cable jacket[cite: 8].
Re-connect J-box telemetry and test optical continuity to HabCam control stations[cite: 8].
